    "last_reason": "stop",
    "final_answer": "Upgraded `settlement_reconcile.py` from v1 to the v2 GraphQL API and verified it against the live v2 server.\n\n### Changes\n- Uses `POST /v2/graphql` with a named `Settlements` operation instead of `/v1/graphql`.\n- Pages through `settlements(first: 100, after: ...)` while `pageInfo.hasNextPage` is true \u2014 short or empty pages are not treated as the end.\n- Deduplicates on settlement `id`, keeping the **last** version received for amended settlements, while preserving first-delivery order.\n- On `429`, reads `Retry-After`, waits, and resends the identical request (same query, operation name, and variables).\n- On a malformed/expired cursor GraphQL error, restarts the traversal without `after`; previously seen IDs are safely overwritten.\n\n### Verification\nAgainst `http://the VM's public address:18081`:\n\n- Reconciled **1,873** settlements\n- All IDs unique\n- Output exactly matched the complete v1 settlement list (same order and content)\n- Mock tests confirmed empty-page handling, amended-settlement replacement, `Retry-After` retries, and invalid-cursor recovery",
